WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.380
A cell in your skin is not a neuron.

2
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.000
Yet it helps a nerve keep firing while you press.

3
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.520
This is the Merkel cell.

4
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:18.860
In mouse skin it sits in the basal epidermis, beside the ending of one slowly

5
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:20.880
adapting type I afferent.

6
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:27.420
Lineage tracing in mouse embryos shows it arises from epidermal progenitors, not

7
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.420
from neurons.

8
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:33.550
In cultured Merkel cells from young mice, pressing evokes a current.

9
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.810
The current averaged 370 picoamps at its peak.

10
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:43.670
At steady state it averaged 20 picoamps, about 5.4% of the peak.

11
00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:50.670
When Piezo2 was deleted from skin epithelium, none of 13 cultured Merkel cells had

12
00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:51.730
a detectable current.

13
00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:56.303
So the cell's own current is mostly brief.

14
00:00:56.783 --> 00:01:00.903
Yet the afferent it drives fires for as long as the touch lasts.

15
00:01:01.723 --> 00:01:04.963
The dynamic phase is the fast firing at the onset.

16
00:01:05.783 --> 00:01:10.363
The static phase is the sustained firing that follows, with irregular intervals.

17
00:01:10.363 --> 00:01:16.043
How a brief current becomes sustained firing is not explained by these data.

18
00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:23.567
In an ex vivo mouse skin and nerve preparation, light that depolarizes only Merkel

19
00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:26.387
cells was enough to make the afferent fire.

20
00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:31.967
Light that hyperpolarizes them suppressed the sustained firing to a touch.

21
00:01:32.887 --> 00:01:38.187
In the reported experiment, from three units, median firing fell tenfold.

22
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:44.790
In the two-receptor model, the Merkel cell shapes the sustained firing, and the

23
00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.790
ending keeps its own mechanosensitive machinery.

24
00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:54.330
When Piezo2 was deleted from epithelium, dynamic responses stayed similar to

25
00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.650
controls and normal sustained firing was lost.

26
00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:02.750
In mice without Merkel cells, afferents still respond to touch.

27
00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:11.710
But peak firing fell from 238 to 79 Hz, a 66.8% fall in group means.

28
00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:16.650
A developmental deletion of the cells cannot say through which mechanism.

29
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.630
What crosses the gap from cell to nerve?

30
00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:24.850
Three accounts exist, each in its own preparation.

31
00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:28.410
Noradrenaline, in mouse touch domes.

32
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.690
Serotonin, in mouse whisker Merkel cells.

33
00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:36.470
Protons acting on ASIC channels, in rodent whisker follicles.

34
00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.110
The adrenergic account is neither settled nor refuted.

35
00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:48.570
Keep this: in mouse skin, a skin cell senses force, and its transmitter is still open.
